Fix lib32-nettle: 32-bit ECC TLS aborts in _nettle_ecc_mod_random

The Arch `lib32-nettle` PKGBUILD configures nettle with the option
`--with-include-path=/usr/lib32/gmp`. nettle 4.0 DELETED that option
(nettle NEWS: "The unusual configure options --with-lib-path and
--with-include-path has been deleted. Use CFLAGS and LDFLAGS");
`configure` now silently ignores it ("WARNING: unrecognized options").

Consequence: the 32-bit build no longer sees the 32-bit gmp.h
(GMP_LIMB_BITS == 32) that lib32-gmp ships at /usr/lib32/gmp/gmp.h.
configure's `AC_COMPUTE_INT(GMP_NUMB_BITS, [#include <gmp.h>])` reads
the 64-bit /usr/include/gmp.h instead and sets NUMB_BITS=64. The
`eccdata` build tool then generates every ECC constant table for
64-bit limbs. In the resulting 32-bit library `struct ecc_modulo.size`
is half the real 32-bit limb count (P-256: 4 instead of 8), so

    ecc-random.c:62  assert (nbytes <= m->size * sizeof (mp_limb_t));

fails -- nbytes=32, m->size*4 = 16 -- and the process ABORTS on every
NIST-curve key generation. All 32-bit ECDSA/ECDH TLS is broken.

Fix: pass the 32-bit gmp include directory via CPPFLAGS, as nettle 4.0
documents. Then NUMB_BITS=32, eccdata generates correct 32-bit tables,
ecc_modulo.size = 8 for P-256, and the assertion is legitimately
satisfied (32 <= 8*4). No nettle source is changed; no assertion or
bounds check is weakened. Verified: nettle's full 32-bit testsuite
passes (All 116 tests passed).

Report this to Arch (bugs.archlinux.org / the lib32-nettle package),
not to nettle upstream -- nettle removed the option deliberately and
documented the replacement.

--- a/PKGBUILD
+++ b/PKGBUILD
@@ -25,9 +25,20 @@
   export CC="gcc -m32"
   export CXX="g++ -m32"
   export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="/usr/lib32/pkgconfig"
+  # nettle >= 4.0 removed the --with-include-path configure option
+  # (see nettle NEWS: "use CFLAGS and LDFLAGS"). The 32-bit build must
+  # still reach the 32-bit gmp.h (GMP_LIMB_BITS == 32) shipped by
+  # lib32-gmp at /usr/lib32/gmp. Without it, configure picks up the
+  # 64-bit /usr/include/gmp.h, detects NUMB_BITS=64, and the eccdata
+  # tool generates the ECC constant tables for 64-bit limbs. The
+  # resulting 32-bit library has ecc_modulo.size at half the limb
+  # count and aborts in _nettle_ecc_mod_random() (ecc-random.c) on
+  # every NIST-curve key generation -- breaking all 32-bit ECDSA/ECDH
+  # TLS. Pass the include directory via CPPFLAGS, as nettle now expects.
+  export CPPFLAGS="-I/usr/lib32/gmp${CPPFLAGS:+ $CPPFLAGS}"

   ./configure --prefix=/usr --libdir=/usr/lib32 \
-    --enable-shared --with-include-path=/usr/lib32/gmp
+    --enable-shared
   make
 }

